# Cutting a release {#s-top}

Start from a clean tree. A release built from uncommitted work cannot be
reproduced, and the version it claims will be a lie.

=== code {#s-cmd lang=sh}
git status --porcelain   # must print nothing
npm publish --access public
===

Confirm the registry actually has it before announcing anything.

## Where each artifact lands {#s-where}

=== table {#s-artifacts caption="One release, four destinations" format=csv header=1}
Artifact, Registry, Confirm with
The parser, npm, a version query
The editor extension, Open VSX, the public API
The browser extension, the Chrome Web Store, a manual upload
===

If any row cannot be confirmed, stop and fix it. A half-published release is
worse than a late one.
